        "question_text": "<p>What is the most effective way to prevent <b>end checking</b> in timber during seasoning?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>End checking occurs when the ends of timber dry faster than the rest of the wood, causing splits. Applying a moisture-resistant sealant or paint to the ends slows down moisture loss, allowing the timber to dry evenly and reducing the risk of checking.</p>",
